#### important interview question:-

Q1. What is the difference between single-threaded and multi-threaded programs?
A:
Single-threaded programs run one task at a time using only the main thread.
Multi-threaded programs use multiple threads to run different tasks at the same time within the same application.

Q2. When would you prefer using a single-threaded program?
A:
When the application is small, doesn't need to multitask, or must run in a specific order - like calculators, simple
notepads, or step-by-step data processing.

Q3. Why is multi-threading useful in real-world applications?
A:
It makes programs faster and more responsive. For example, a music app plays songs, shows lyrics, and loads the next
track at the same time without freezing - thanks to multithreading.
